  ('the-brownstone', 'series', 'published', 'The Brownstone', 2023, '3 Seasons', ARRAY['Drama'], 'United States', 'English', 'Five queer New Yorkers share a rent-controlled brownstone that''s rapidly becoming the last one on the block, and over three seasons they build the kind of family none of them were handed at birth. Careers rise and stall, relationships form and collapse, and the building itself keeps threatening to be sold out from under them — but every season ends the same way: around the same kitchen table, further apart in life and closer to each other than they started.', 'Four floors. One family that isn''t related by blood.', 4.7, NULL, 'Priya Nathan', ARRAY['Jordan Lee', 'Marcus Bell', 'Ines Okafor', 'Theo Diaz', 'Dana Ruiz'], ARRAY['Found Family', 'Ensemble', 'LGBTQ+', 'New York'], DATE '2023-04-11', NULL, 'https://picsum.photos/seed/the-brownstone/500/750', NULL, 'from-pride-blue to-pride-purple', false, 0, now() - interval '1440 hours', now() - interval '1 hours'),
  ('friend-of-dorothy', 'series', 'published', 'Friend of Dorothy', 2024, '2 Seasons', ARRAY['Comedy'], 'United States', 'English', 'The last lesbian bar in a shrinking downtown scene becomes an unlikely home base for a group of regulars spanning three generations — a Gen Z bartender figuring out who she is, a Gen X owner trying to keep the lights on, and a Boomer regular who''s been on the same stool since 1994. Funny, messy, and unashamedly niche, Friend of Dorothy is about what it means to hold onto a space that was never supposed to still exist.', 'Every generation needs a bar to call home.', 4.4, NULL, 'Devon Okafor', ARRAY['Riley Chen', 'Claire Whitfield', 'Nadia Torres', 'Sam Park'], ARRAY['Bar', 'Multigenerational', 'LGBTQ+', 'Comedy'], DATE '2024-07-09', NULL, 'https://picsum.photos/seed/friend-of-dorothy/500/750', NULL, 'from-pride-yellow to-pride-red', false, 0, now() - interval '1464 hours', now() - interval '2 hours'),
